From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iván Ruiz <iruizl2004@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:38:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2157/2160] firmware: arm_scmi: perf: Do not mark all OPPs
 turbo without a sustained frequency

On the Snapdragon X Plus X1P-64-100, two of the three CPU clusters have
a core fused off. The CPUCP firmware reports a sustained frequency of 0
for their performance domains, as it finds no sustained-frequency entry
for their core count. scmi_dvfs_device_opps_add() then flags every OPP
of those domains as turbo, cpufreq_table_validate_and_sort() finds no
non-boost frequency and fails with -EINVAL, and the CPUs in those
clusters (6 of 10 on the Surface Pro 11) get no cpufreq policy at all.
The failure is only visible at debug level.

A domain without a sustained frequency has no turbo threshold, so mark
none of its OPPs turbo. The multiplier computation above already treats
a zero sustained frequency as "not provided".

With this, a Surface Pro 11 X Plus gets a cpufreq policy for each of
its three clusters.

Fixes: a897575e79d7 ("firmware: arm_scmi: Add support for marking certain frequencies as turbo")
Link: https://github.com/dwhinham/archiso-aarch64-sp11/issues/36
Assisted-by: LLM

---
 drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
index 4583d02be..482a82733 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
@@ -879,8 +879,14 @@ static int scmi_dvfs_device_opps_add(const struct scmi_protocol_handle *ph,
 		else
 			freq = dom->opp[idx].indicative_freq * dom->mult_factor;
 
-		/* All OPPs above the sustained frequency are treated as turbo */
-		data.turbo = freq > dom->sustained_freq_khz * 1000UL;
+		/*
+		 * All OPPs above the sustained frequency are treated as turbo.
+		 * A domain that reports no sustained frequency has no such
+		 * threshold: marking every OPP turbo would leave cpufreq with
+		 * no usable frequency, and the policy would not be created.
+		 */
+		data.turbo = dom->sustained_freq_khz &&
+			     freq > dom->sustained_freq_khz * 1000UL;
 
 		data.level = dom->opp[idx].perf;
 		data.freq = freq;
-- 
